The code statements that lead to the bug are:
do { *--frag = *--frag2; } while (--i);
memcpy(frag + 1, skbinfo->frags, sizeof(*frag) * skbinfo->nr_frags);
Reason:
These fragment copy operations in `skb_gro_receive` assume normal page refcounting. For zerocopy skbs (with `SKBFL_MANAGED_FRAG_REFS` set), pages are not refcounted individually; copying frags without adjusting refs leads to a use-after-free when the original skb releases its pages.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (skb_zcopy(p) || skb_zcopy(skb))
    return -ETOOMANYREFS;
Reason:
This early check prevents merging when either the GRO skb (`p`) or the source skb (`skb`) is zerocopy, avoiding unsafe fragment copying and thus eliminating the UAF condition.

